{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Software and Hardware Engineer"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about software and hardware."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understand important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.  Exchange simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Tense Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span> to talk about duties and occupations. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I work as a hardware engineer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Software engineers need to be more creative than hardware engineers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To make affirmative statements in <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span>, you just need to follow the next structure:<br/><br/>  Subject  + <span class=\"strong\">Verb</span> + Complement<br/><br/>  Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">They <span class=\"strong\">work</span> as engineers in a software company.</span><br/><br/>  Remember that If the subject pronoun is <span class=\"strong\">he, she</span> or <span class=\"strong\">it</span>, you must add the letter s at the end of the verb.<br/><br/>  Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Sam <span class=\"strong\">works</span> as an engineer in a software company.<br/><br/>  In some cases, you will need to add <span class=\"strong\">-es</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ies</span> to the verb. Take a look at the following chart:<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Rule</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Examples</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Most verbs just need <span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"design - design<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span><br/> produce - produce<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span><br/> train - train<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Add <span class=\\\"strong\\\">es</span> to verbs that end in: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">ch, sh, o</span> and <span class=\\\"italic\\\">x</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"watch - watch<span class=\\\"strong\\\">es</span><br/> wash  - wash<span class=\\\"strong\\\">es</span><br/> go - go<span class=\\\"strong\\\">es</span> <br/> fix - fix<span class=\\\"strong\\\">es</span><br/>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Add <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ies</span> to verbs that end in a consonant + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">y</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"study - stud<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ies</span><br/> cry  - cr<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ies</span><br/> carry  - carr<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ies</span><br/>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Add <span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span if the verb ends in a <span class=\\\"italic\\\">vowel</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">y</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pl<span class=\\\"underline\\\">ay</span>  - play<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span><br/> b<span class=\\\"underline\\\">uy</span>  - buy<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span><br/> s<span class=\\\"underline\\\">ay</span>  - say<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think technical responsibilities are more important for you than programming responsibilities. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Idioms about Technology"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We can find different expressions and idioms that contain vocabulary related to technology. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that we shouldn't deduce the meaning of an idiom by the meaning of the word in it. Instead, we need to memorize what it really mean. Let's take a look at some examples of idioms: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\">To blow a fuse</span> means to become really angry about something.<br/><br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">Harry, <span class=\"strong\">don't blow a fuse</span>. I didn't mean to break your mouse. </span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Cog in the machine</span> refers to someone with little importance in a big organization.<br/><br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">I don't want to be just <span class=\"strong\">a cog in the machine</span>. I want to have more responsibilities.</span><br/><br/>   <span class=\"strong\">To hit the panic button</span> means to lose control and panic. <br/><br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">We don't know how to fix this software. But we are not going <span class=\"strong\">to hit the panic button</span> yet.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hardware "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "components of a computer, such as the hard disk drive, the monitor, the keyboard and others"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have to check the hardware configuration of computers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "research"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an investigation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are more skillful in research than us."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "support "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a service assistance and supervision "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I handle support all the time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "skillful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "experienced and competent "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are more skillful in research than us."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "database"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a system that contains information "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Main duties and responsibilities of that job are related to networks and database management."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "keep up to date "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be informed all the time about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to keep up to date on technology advancements."}, {"type": "audio", "content"